Showcase_Hub_MayorsOffice=The Mayor's Office
Showcase_HubEarly_HospitalBody=A visit here may reveal the source of the fever, at some cost to your composure.
Showcase_HubEarly_LibraryBody=Knowledge awaits those patient enough to read every dusty volume.
Showcase_HubMiddle_BuildHospitalBody=The church can no longer handle the influx of the diseased. Each visit may fund a new wing, at a cost.
Showcase_HubMiddle_SecondRoundEventBody=Political pandering may require extra capital on hand, should the need arise.
Showcase_HubMiddle_AngryMobBody=Suspicion has taken root among the townsfolk. Left unaddressed, it will not stay quiet for long.
Showcase_HubLate_LibraryBody=A new Library has been built in town. For each visit, gain one Knowledge of your choice.
Showcase_HubLate_BuildHospitalBody=The church can no longer handle the influx of the diseased and needs to expand its facilities.
Showcase_HubLate_AngryMobBody=Clandestine meetings continue in the old mill. When a player reveals their Sealed Envelope card, click here for a special secret message.
Showcase_HubLate_ReliefBody=A completed Experiment can be used to ignore all ill effects from Disease between rounds.
Showcase_HubLate_MayorsOfficeBody=The election looms. Whoever bids the most will hold the office until the family's work is done — or undone.

Showcase_Reveal_Title=Reveal Popup
Showcase_Reveal_Label=Once you are ready, click here to reveal your secret conversation.
Showcase_Reveal_Heading=**A Seedy Arrangement**
Showcase_Reveal_Recall="You will recall," the letter began, "our conversations in the amphitheatre, before the faculty grew tiresome of our methods. I write now not out of nostalgia, but out of necessity -- I have found something in the old records that I believe belongs to your particular expertise, and to no one else's."
Showcase_Reveal_Accustomed=The household had grown accustomed to such letters by now -- invitations to obscurity dressed up as academic curiosity, forwarded from one estranged colleague to the next until they found a family willing to entertain them. Most were discarded within the hour. This one was not.
Showcase_Reveal_Evening=By evening, the notation had been transcribed twice, cross-referenced against the family's own considerable library, and pinned to the wall of the study alongside a dozen other threads that had, over the years, refused to resolve into anything resembling an answer.
Showcase_Reveal_Representative=A representative arrived within the week, unannounced, and was received all the same. Their mannerisms were especially secretive and plotting, though their offer -- once made -- was plain enough: support, substantial and immediate, in exchange for nothing more than a favor to be named later. It was, they noted with an unsettling grin, always easier to ask a friend than a stranger.
Showcase_Reveal_Choose=**CHOOSE:**
Showcase_Reveal_Accept=Accept the offer.
Showcase_Reveal_AcceptNote=(To gain $2.)
Showcase_Reveal_Or=OR
Showcase_Reveal_Refuse=Refuse the offer.
Showcase_Reveal_RefuseNote=(To avoid a debt in the future.)

Showcase_Countdown_Title=Reveal Countdown Popup
Showcase_Countdown_Intro=A genuinely nested popup: the outer note holds the instructions and never closes on its own — the inner popup's own trigger button sits inline in its content, and its Okay button is invisible and full-screen until a CSS countdown finishes.
Showcase_Countdown_Label=click to start the bid...
Showcase_Countdown_Body1=Click on the 'Start Bidding' button to start the bid. This will start a 3-second countdown.
Showcase_Countdown_Body2=When you see the word 'REVEAL' on the screen, simultaneously show everyone your bid.
Showcase_Countdown_StartBidding=Start Bidding

